        "@value": "&lt;p&gt;Created in 2024 by comedians Hilary Henderson and Michelle Forrester, Pink Chicken features an all-female lineup of standup comedians and a one-of-a-kind interactive audience segment.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Our interactive crowd segment invites audience members to share their boldest takes on the issues plaguing our modern world (from dating to mother wounds; no two shows are the same!) Topics usually revolve around mental health, self care, work, family, dating, relationships, and anything else pertaining to the female experience.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Through the shared experience of laughter, Pink Chicken curates an inclusive environment where no submission is too dark, embarrassing, or weird. Pink Chicken is the IRL community replicated from your funniest text exchanges.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Fresh off the heels of a successful run at Edmonton Fringe Festival, Hilary and Michelle bring their silliest, most unapologetic group chat energy to every stage they possibly can!&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;#8212;&lt;br /&gt;\nABOUT YOUR HOSTS&lt;br /&gt;\nHilary&amp;#8217;s original comedic content has racked up over millions of views and has been featured in Narcity Canada, Yahoo Lifestyle, and girlie&amp;#8217;s group chats across the world! She has performed standup across Canada and has opened for acts featured on Comedy Central, Jimmy Fallon, Just for Laughs, and CBC Comedy.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Michelle is a Canadian comic and writer born in Montreal. In 2023, she moved to Toronto to complete an MFA in Screenwriting at Toronto Metropolitan University where she co-created The Writers Room Sketch Show &amp;#8211; a project that went on to win first place at the JFL Stand-Up and Pitch Contest. And In 2023, she was also named a New Face of Comedy by Just For Laughs. In 2022, she recorded on the JFL Originals album &amp;#8220;Heavy Petting Zoo.&amp;#8221; She will definitely beat you at a hot dog eating contest.&lt;/p&gt;\n"
